WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.456 --> 00:00:05.118
Danny: Okay.

2
00:00:13.142 --> 00:00:16.844
explore! Brad: Let’s stick together this time.

3
00:00:16.864 --> 00:00:19.966
Danny: I think that’s a safe rule to follow.

4
00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:22.107
Tina: Follow me, boys!

5
00:00:22.127 --> 00:00:26.830
Tina: Look at this beautiful garden!

6
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.352
Tina: Have you ever seen anything like it?

7
00:00:30.044 --> 00:00:30.845
Danny: Never.

8
00:00:31.165 --> 00:00:33.647
There are more flowers than I’ve ever seen!

9
00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:35.268
Brad: Ah-choo!

10
00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:38.191
Tina: What’s the matter, Brad?

11
00:00:39.112 --> 00:00:41.193
Brad: Allergies.

12
00:00:41.213 --> 00:00:43.715
Danny: You’re allergic to flowers?

13
00:00:44.656 --> 00:00:45.477
Brad: I’ll be okay.

14
00:00:45.897 --> 00:00:47.819
It’s just a little tickle in my nose.

15
00:00:48.659 --> 00:00:58.868
Brad: But I guess when there are so many Tina: We'd better find a way out of here.

16
00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.021
Danny: Hey, what’s that over there?

17
00:01:02.041 --> 00:01:04.682
Tina: It looks like apple trees!

18
00:01:04.702 --> 00:01:07.403
Danny: I am so hungry!

19
00:01:07.423 --> 00:01:10.144
Tina: I could eat a whole tree!

20
00:01:10.164 --> 00:01:18.908
Danny: Here, Brad, try an apple.

21
00:01:18.928 --> 00:01:24.130
Brad: I prefer oranges.

22
00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.431
Danny: Where did you find that?

23
00:01:26.451 --> 00:01:28.672
Tina: Over here, Danny!

24
00:01:30.028 --> 00:01:33.791
Brad: Follow me.

25
00:01:33.811 --> 00:01:34.891
Tina: Look!

26
00:01:35.072 --> 00:01:36.933
There’s a whole bunch of orange trees too!

27
00:01:36.993 --> 00:01:39.935
Brad: And over here, there are lemon trees!

28
00:01:39.955 --> 00:01:42.577
Danny: What’s that over there?

29
00:01:42.597 --> 00:01:44.898
Tina Brad: Bananas!

30
00:01:45.919 --> 00:01:49.141
Brad: Do you still think this is the giants’ world, Danny?

31
00:01:49.161 --> 00:01:50.702
Danny: No.

32
00:01:50.982 --> 00:01:52.343
It’s too colorful.

33
00:01:52.924 --> 00:01:53.864
So what should we do?

34
00:01:53.884 --> 00:01:56.886
Tina: Stay here and eat forever?

35
00:01:59.180 --> 00:01:59.740
Brad: Ah-choo!

36
00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:01.621
I don’t think that will work for me.

37
00:02:01.641 --> 00:02:04.242
Tina: Right.

38
00:02:04.642 --> 00:02:06.263
Well, where do we go next?

39
00:02:06.283 --> 00:02:09.144
Danny: Let’s think about this for a minute.

40
00:02:09.164 --> 00:02:13.126
Danny: The blue key got us to a world full of water.

41
00:02:13.146 --> 00:02:16.868
Brad: The red key brought us to a world full of snow.

42
00:02:16.888 --> 00:02:21.290
Tina: But really it is a world of flowers and fruit!

43
00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:23.971
Brad: Right.

44
00:02:24.531 --> 00:02:26.632
Danny, what other colors do you have?

45
00:02:28.652 --> 00:02:29.292
Danny: Yellow.

46
00:02:30.753 --> 00:02:33.313
Tina: Yellow.

47
00:02:33.713 --> 00:02:35.074
Brad: Yellow.

48
00:02:35.094 --> 00:02:37.054
Danny: What does it mean?

49
00:02:37.074 --> 00:02:42.116
Brad: Do you think the yellow clay is the key to the giants’ world?

50
00:02:42.136 --> 00:02:44.116
Danny: I don’t know.

51
00:02:44.676 --> 00:02:46.397
What else could yellow be for?

52
00:02:46.417 --> 00:02:47.837
Tina: Bananas?

53
00:02:47.857 --> 00:02:50.658
Brad: The point is we just don’t know.

54
00:02:50.678 --> 00:02:54.459
Brad: Do we want to take the chance again?

55
00:02:54.479 --> 00:02:57.760
Danny: What other choice do we have?

56
00:02:58.816 --> 00:02:59.557
Tina: Danny’s right.

57
00:02:59.817 --> 00:03:01.479
We don’t even know how to get home.

58
00:03:01.499 --> 00:03:04.702
Brad: So we need to try the yellow clay?

59
00:03:04.722 --> 00:03:07.325
Agreed? Danny Tina: Agreed!
